4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T21:49:48-08:00","id":809372,"title":"","content":"Buddha: &quot;Yo.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:22:23-08:00","id":809835,"title":"","content":"The implication I got is that <i>nobody</i> gets into A'aru, at least not if the Judges have anything to say about it. By Sutek's decree, they can only feed sinners to Ammut -- so they try to make sure everyone is a sinner. The laws they enforce are deliberately designed to trip up as many people as possible. Remember that the original purpose of the Temakhs was to <i>teach people how to sin.</i> (And they were exceptionally good teachers, even after they rebelled.)<br /> <br /> The whole game is <i>rigged.</i> And Sutek, or what's left of him, is not happy about it. Which is why he's trying to guide the Deathless to Apotheosis -- so they can bring the whole corrupt system down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:59:12-08:00","id":811218,"title":"","content":"Maybe it is a setting to build a new world. Or a safe place, relatively speaking of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T11:59:42-08:00","id":811245,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I'm wrong, but even if every Deathless reaches Apotheosis, wouldn't Ammut still win? She'd still eventually eat all the Sekhem out there, which probably means saying good-bye to living things as we recognize them. And the Apotheosis-ized Deathless would no longer be <i>quite </i>so Deathless. Who would be left to oppose Ammut? The Deceived?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:19:27-08:00","id":811252,"title":"","content":"Not cessinarily. A'aru, as Sutek describes it, seems to exist in defiance of Ammut and the Judges.<br /> <br /> But that possibility aside, Ammut wins in all scenarios, but the question isn't &quot;Can we beat Ammut?&quot;, it's &quot;Can we beat the Judges and the Shan'iatu before Ammut wins?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:52:01-08:00","id":811269,"title":"","content":"Ah, so Sutek trying to get people to A'aru is more or less a noble delay tactic than a potential win? One of those &quot;better to have tried and failed&quot; type situations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:01:32-08:00","id":818760,"title":"","content":"I finished the book, so yeah A'aru seems to reflect the Empyrean, and it is a place where you are free from enslavement. The Book of Ages seems to be the Supernal itself, hence writing and reading from it effects the Phenomenal.<br /> <br /> More importantly it may be barren because the Judges and Shan'iatu seem to not be letting people in, and do their best to keep people out and delay them. The Heretic may be seening this as the first, or at least one of the first, Arisen to enter A'aru. He is to light the way for others and they may till the barren soil into a heaven. He seemed to realize the ways of the Religion of Irem were not righteous ways, not ways to lead humanity, but they were ways you could see what was and wasn't righteous through meditating on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T18:28:55-08:00","id":820069,"title":"","content":"How big a spoilsport am I? This big.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmmm...so hauntingly beautiful yet utterly empty mansions (and the city Amenti?) hidden beyond the reach of the living and by and large the dead, beyond even the ken of nothingness incarnate, filled with stars that are not stars and secret words that can shape the face of reality or drive men mad. What does this remind me of?....or yeah. Carcosa. This sounds like the vague and brief descriptions from the King in Yellow. Hey, doesn't Mummy have an Ochre Masked King? One that gets banished to an unfathomable 'hell' when his name is erased by powerful Nomenclature every 1000 years? Why yes, I believe it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> In addition, A'aru is said to be accessible solely by the Judges and seems to be the key to some of their plans. The Judges are merciless, enigmatic entities who cannot be looked upon directly for their true forms cannot be fathomed by the minds of mortals or Mummies. Are we so sure that journeying to this place they covet for themselves is a good thing? These are uncaring god-things who answered the question 'What is the meaning of life?' with 'To Suffer'. They covet A'aru...and that's a good thing? Are we prepared to say that what the Judges want for themselves is something humanity should claim? This is where the Scroll of Ages shines in the night sky, right? The Scroll of all things, with words that not only describe but ARE the underpinnings of all reality, that contains the secrets of existence and the truths underpinning reality itself. Is humanity, or the Arisen, prepared to read those words and know those truths? <br /> <br /> Or put it yet another way. A'aru is, arguably, the place where all of Irem's magic began. The stars in its sky are the Words from which all Hekau are drawn- every art of the Guild has its basis in the Scroll. So when has anything Iremite ever, EVER, allowed its magic to be worked without a curse? A'aru sits overhead, waiting for the doors to open, waiting for the purest, ultimate, first curse to issue forth...waiting for THE CURSE to fall upon the world. <br /> <br /> \u200bHave fun climbing the ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:00:15-08:00","id":820475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/808197-starry-a-aru?p=811252#post811252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not cessinarily. A'aru, as Sutek describes it, seems to exist in defiance of Ammut and the Judges.<br /> <br /> But that possibility aside, Ammut wins in all scenarios, but the question isn't &quot;Can we beat Ammut?&quot;, it's &quot;Can we beat the Judges and the Shan'iatu before Ammut wins?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Trying to beat Ammut is like trying to beat the heat-death of the universe, you can't escape it. All you can do is do the best in the time you have. Which means beating the Judges and Shan'iatu ASAP and thereafter stalling Ammut as long as possible and living life to the fullest in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T11:23:40-08:00","id":843057,"title":"","content":"Khepera notes that all things contain him <b>except</b> A'aru. Khepera is balanced in the jaws of Ammut, but A'aru isn't. Meaning that when she with teeth like mountains wins A'aru will still be there. It is a bomb shelter that will survive the destruction of the world. If the Scroll of Ages is the Supernal it is also the location from which a new world can be created.<br /> <br /> However, since Nu is also within the jaws of Ammut, I suspect that only A'aru/the Empyrean/Supernal is free from the predations of the Abyss/Ammut and all possible worlds must necessarily be imperfect reflections and subject to decay.<br /> <br /> So the world is meant to create things worthy and able to enter starry A'aru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T11:44:44-08:00","id":843071,"title":"","content":"Well it <i>is</i> the sky above the skies, where people may at last find purchase from the inescapable. But rather than the meaning of the world, I would call it the meaning above inevitability for the sake of which Sutek stood against the Law of Suffering. The hope he dreamed of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-06-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:59:40-08:00","id":844393,"title":"","content":"The impression I get, honestly, is that A'aru is actually beyond the reach of the Judges. The Temakh who narrates the introduction to the <i>Book of the </i><i>Deceived</i> certainly <i>believed</i> that the Judges ruled from A'aru, but as we've seen, the Shan'iatu were mistaken about a great many things. All the Judges seem to be able to do is bar entry to others, but those with sufficient Will can press past them. Indeed, Sutekh explicitly describes the gates of A'aru as &quot;beyond&quot; the Judges, and says that those who look upon the sky beyond the sky will see &quot;why [they] are alone.&quot; Along with the reference to A'aru's fields being barren, this seems to suggest that the place is empty save for those who climb to it by Sutekh's ladder.<br /> <br /> But A'aru clearly isn't <i>just</i> empty. Sutekh doesn't describe the fields as deserted, or fallow, but rather <i>barren</i>, as in infertile, incapable of bearing life. I get the sense that something is terribly wrongwith the order of the cosmos if A'aru's fields are barren. Maybe the Heretic isn't just a sort of Deathless Bodhisattva, forsaking paradise in order to help others reach Apotheosis. Maybe Apotheosis is only the first step; maybe once the Deathless have seen &quot;why the fields are barren,&quot; they'll have some inkling of what might be done to restore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:45:57-08:00","id":844433,"title":"","content":"I like that it's barren. There's a peacefulness and tranquility in thoughtlessness and emptiness, and even if that's not why it's presented as barren I think the Arisen have a good cause to desire A'aru still. They've (probably literally) been through hell and back, unlived through all of history, fought demons, died just to come back to life, and have have limbs eaten by Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> That's a hell of a fight, and knowing that there's <i>just a break to take</i> at the end of the road is a relief","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:39:37-08:00","id":844604,"title":"","content":"Maybe my reading is flawed, but I saw A'aru as barren simply because no one was reaching it and bringing their Sekhem with them; humanity hasn't known the way for thousands of years, and only one of the Arisen has pulled it off. If those two things were made right, I can see it flourishing once more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T08:26:32-07:00","id":866392,"title":"","content":"Just an offhand thought, but what if we aren't looking at this literally enough. What if A'aru is literally a barren world (or barren worlds) among the stars where I the Fifth Turn the Arisen can finally reach outside the earthbound metaphysical grasp of their masters? This is all heading toward religious Exodus space-opera...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}